// A **native** expression tier (expr-tiers arc E6b): `@json` is declared by std through the
// extension `ExtTier` surface — no `.noe` file declares it and nothing is imported — with a
// *native* handler (`std.template.render`). A `@json { … ${s} … }` block desugars to that handler
// call through the identical path a program (Noeta-fn) handler uses: the callee is just a resolved
// native function value (`NativeFnRef` → `Const::ModuleFn`). The handler interleaves the verbatim
// statics with the JSON-quoted string holes. Both backends agree by construction (the differential
// oracle) — the reference interpreter and the VM share the module-function value and dispatch.
// expect: stdout " {"id": "u-7", "name": "Ada Lovelace"} "
// expect: exit 0
id = "u-7"
name = "Ada Lovelace"
doc = @json { {"id": ${id}, "name": ${name}} }
echo doc
